[2026-02-04T17:19:10.820Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wZqWVDHNCa1xbgTjwYAXe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SEC AI-washing enforcement actions securities fraud artificial intelligence misrepresentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SEC.gov | SEC Charges Two Investment Advisers with Making False and Misleading Statements About Their Use of Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2024-36\"},{\"title\":\"SEC and DOJ Warm Up to Enforcement over AI Washing | Insights | Holland & Knight\",\"url\":\"https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/07/sec-and-doj-warm-up-to-enforcement-over-ai-washing\"},{\"title\":\"Regulating AI Deception in Financial Markets: How the SEC Can Combat AI-Washing Through Aggressive Enforcement - New York State Bar Association\",\"url\":\"https://nysba.org/regulating-ai-deception-in-financial-markets-how-the-sec-can-combat-ai-washing-through-aggressive-enforcement/\"},{\"title\":\"SEC emphasizes focus on “AI washing” despite perceived enforcement slowdown | DLA Piper\",\"url\":\"https://www.dlapiper.com/en/insights/publications/ai-outlook/2025/sec-emphasizes-focus-on-ai-washing\"},{\"title\":\"SEC Announces First-Ever Enforcement Actions for “AI ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lw.com/admin/upload/SiteAttachments/SEC-Announces-First-Ever-Enforcement-Actions-for-AI-Washing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Securities and Exchange Commission Brings First Enforcement Actions Over “AI-Washing” | Insights | Mayer Brown\",\"url\":\"https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2024/04/securities-and-exchange-commission-brings-first-enforcement-actions-over-aiwashing\"},{\"title\":\"SEC Fines Two Investment Advisers for “AI Washing”\",\"url\":\"https://corpgov.law.harvard.edu/2024/04/09/sec-fines-two-investment-advisers-for-ai-washing/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Enforcement Starts with Washing: The SEC Charges its First AI Fraud Cases – Debevoise Data Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.debevoisedatablog.com/2024/03/19/ai-enforcement-starts-with-washing-the-sec-charges-its-first-ai-fraud-cases/\"},{\"title\":\"New Settlements Demonstrate the SEC’s Ongoing Efforts to Hold Companies Accountable for AI-Washing | White & Case LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/new-settlements-demonstrate-secs-ongoing-efforts-hold-companies-accountable-ai\"},{\"title\":\"Artificial Intelligence or Illusions: The SEC’s Crackdown on Misleading AI Claims — the RACE to the BOTTOM\",\"url\":\"https://www.theracetothebottom.org/rttb/2025/3/31/artificial-intelligence-or-illusions-the-secs-crackdown-on-misleading-ai-claims\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about SEC enforcement actions related to AI-washing and securities fraud. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key SEC Enforcement Actions\n\n### Delphia and Global Predictions Settlement (March 2024)\n\nThe SEC announced settled charges against two investment advisers, Delphia (USA) Inc. and Global Predictions Inc., for making false and misleading statements about their purported use of artificial intelligence (AI). The firms agreed to settle the SEC's charges and pay $400,000 in total civil penalties.\n\nFor example, the firm falsely claimed to be the \"first regulated AI financial advisor\" and misrepresented that its platform provided \"[e]xpert AI-driven forecasts.\" During an examination, the SEC discovered that Delphia had not used any client data, and that it did not have an algorithm to use client data.\n\n### Nate Inc. Case (Criminal & Civil)\n\nThe SEC and DOJ filed parallel actions against Albert Saniger, the founder and former CEO of Nate Inc., alleging that he made false and misleading statements to investors about Nate's purported AI technology, raising more than $42 million over three years. The SEC alleges Saniger knew the app lacked any functional AI model, yet he continued to tout high automation rates to investors, fabricating success metrics claiming automation rates above 90 percent when the automation rate was \"essentially zero.\"\n\n## SEC's Enforcement Posture\n\nSenior officials from the SEC's Enforcement Division and newly constituted Cybersecurity and Emerging Technologies Unit (CETU) reiterated that \"rooting out\" fraud schemes related to \"AI washing\" – referring to a company's materially false and misleading statements about their artificial intelligence (AI) capabilities – is an immediate priority.\n\nSecurities class actions targeting alleged AI misrepresentations have increased by 100% between 2023 and 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"921d87c4-ac45-4160-8b92-92ba1cdd4213","tool_use_result":{"query":"SEC AI-washing enforcement actions securities fraud artificial intelligence misrepresentation","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CkmZCswNBJ8uR6h6L9tCdn","content":[{"title":"SEC.gov | SEC Charges Two Investment Advisers with Making False and Misleading Statements About Their Use of Artificial Intelligence","url":"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2024-36"},{"title":"SEC and DOJ Warm Up to Enforcement over AI Washing | Insights | Holland & Knight","url":"https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2025/07/sec-and-doj-warm-up-to-enforcement-over-ai-washing"},{"title":"Regulating AI Deception in Financial Markets: How the SEC Can Combat AI-Washing Through Aggressive Enforcement - New York State Bar Association","url":"https://nysba.org/regulating-ai-deception-in-financial-markets-how-the-sec-can-combat-ai-washing-through-aggressive-enforcement/"},{"title":"SEC emphasizes focus on “AI washing” despite perceived enforcement slowdown | DLA Piper","url":"https://www.dlapiper.com/en/insights/publications/ai-outlook/2025/sec-emphasizes-focus-on-ai-washing"},{"title":"SEC Announces First-Ever Enforcement Actions for “AI ...","url":"https://www.lw.com/admin/upload/SiteAttachments/SEC-Announces-First-Ever-Enforcement-Actions-for-AI-Washing.pdf"},{"title":"Securities and Exchange Commission Brings First Enforcement Actions Over “AI-Washing” | Insights | Mayer Brown","url":"https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2024/04/securities-and-exchange-commission-brings-first-enforcement-actions-over-aiwashing"},{"title":"SEC Fines Two Investment Advisers for “AI Washing”","url":"https://corpgov.law.harvard.edu/2024/04/09/sec-fines-two-investment-advisers-for-ai-washing/"},{"title":"AI Enforcement Starts with Washing: The SEC Charges its First AI Fraud Cases – Debevoise Data Blog","url":"https://www.debevoisedatablog.com/2024/03/19/ai-enforcement-starts-with-washing-the-sec-charges-its-first-ai-fraud-cases/"},{"title":"New Settlements Demonstrate the SEC’s Ongoing Efforts to Hold Companies Accountable for AI-Washing | White & Case LLP","url":"https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/new-settlements-demonstrate-secs-ongoing-efforts-hold-companies-accountable-ai"},{"title":"Artificial Intelligence or Illusions: The SEC’s Crackdown on Misleading AI Claims — the RACE to the BOTTOM","url":"https://www.theracetothebottom.org/rttb/2025/3/31/artificial-intelligence-or-illusions-the-secs-crackdown-on-misleading-ai-claims"}]},"I've found comprehensive information about SEC enforcement actions related to AI-washing and securities fraud. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key SEC Enforcement Actions\n\n### Delphia and Global Predictions Settlement (March 2024)\n\nThe SEC announced settled charges against two investment advisers, Delphia (USA) Inc. and Global Predictions Inc., for making false and misleading statements about their purported use of artificial intelligence (AI). The firms agreed to settle the SEC's charges and pay $400,000 in total civil penalties.\n\nFor example, the firm falsely claimed to be the \"first regulated AI financial advisor\" and misrepresented that its platform provided \"[e]xpert AI-driven forecasts.\" During an examination, the SEC discovered that Delphia had not used any client data, and that it did not have an algorithm to use client data.\n\n### Nate Inc. Case (Criminal & Civil)\n\nThe SEC and DOJ filed parallel actions against Albert Saniger, the founder and former CEO of Nate Inc., alleging that he made false and misleading statements to investors about Nate's purported AI technology, raising more than $42 million over three years. The SEC alleges Saniger knew the app lacked any functional AI model, yet he continued to tout high automation rates to investors, fabricating success metrics claiming automation rates above 90 percent when the automation rate was \"essentially zero.\"\n\n## SEC's Enforcement Posture\n\nSenior officials from the SEC's Enforcement Division and newly constituted Cybersecurity and Emerging Technologies Unit (CETU) reiterated that \"rooting out\" fraud schemes related to \"AI washing\" – referring to a company's materially false and misleading statements about their artificial intelligence (AI) capabilities – is an immediate priority.\n\nSecurities class actions targeting alleged AI misrepresentations have increased by 100% between 2023 and 2024."],"durationSeconds":8.549392600000001}}
[2026-02-04T17:19:11.384Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Jmq7Boy4ZTGBucn31H2kx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Skadden AI securities litigation trends 2026 class actions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/landing-page\"},{\"title\":\"Securities Litigation | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/capabilities/practices/litigationcontroversy/cc/securities-litigation\"},{\"title\":\"2026 US trends: AI, securities and Delaware disputes - CDR News\",\"url\":\"https://www.cdr-news.com/categories/litigation/2026-us-trends-ai-securities-and-delaware-disputes/\"},{\"title\":\"Inside the Courts – An Update From Skadden Securities Litigators | Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2025/02/inside-the-courts\"},{\"title\":\"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP - JDSupra\",\"url\":\"https://www.jdsupra.com/legalnews/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-5893942/\"},{\"title\":\"M&A in the AI Era: What Buyers Can Do to Confirm and Protect Value | Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/sector-spotlights/ma-in-the-ai-era\"},{\"title\":\"Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom AI: Strategic Positioning in Legal AI - Klover.ai\",\"url\":\"https://www.klover.ai/skadden-arps-slate-meagher-flom-ai-strategic-positioning-in-legal-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights?type=%7B0416A0AE-D175-4993-BBE0-6CF0CF7397DA%7D&capability=8551cacf-412c-4b5f-bfb4-000000037635&hassearched=true&panelid=tab-find-mode\"},{\"title\":\"Don’t Believe the Hype: Government Regulation of AI Continues to Advance | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/sector-spotlights/dont-believe-the-hype\"}]\n\nI found Skadden's analysis of AI-related securities litigation trends for 2026. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overall Litigation Activity\n\nSecurities class action filings remained elevated in 2025, signaling that robust activity will likely persist into 2026.\n\n## AI and Emerging Trends\n\nCurrent securities litigation trends are likely to continue through 2026, with plaintiffs increasingly bringing suits over AI claims and private lending. Additionally, plaintiffs are also testing the limits of when expert opinions and short-seller reports can be credited at the motion-to-dismiss stage.\n\n## Private Credit Market\n\nPrivate credit lenders may become targets in securities class actions arising from capital raises involving retail investors. Plaintiffs have thus far treated private credit vehicles like traditional issuers under Rule 10b-5, focusing on alleged misstatements about portfolio performance and asset values.\n\n## Arbitration Clauses and Class Actions\n\nIf companies take advantage of the SEC's new openness to mandatory arbitration clauses, the securities litigation landscape could be altered, but the firm does not anticipate a flood of companies doing so at this stage. However, plaintiffs' attorneys have already indicated plans to challenge mandatory arbitration provisions if adopted.\n\nThe Skadden analysis emphasizes that the intersection of emerging technologies, regulatory shifts and evolving pleading strategies will present both challenges and opportunities for companies, investors and practitioners alike.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"5fdf4769-1f40-4c91-921b-7520384ba9f6","tool_use_result":{"query":"Skadden AI securities litigation trends 2026 class actions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014JYv9FFiPT3oM2h1pyU6rz","content":[{"title":"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch"},{"title":"2026 Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/landing-page"},{"title":"Securities Litigation | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/capabilities/practices/litigationcontroversy/cc/securities-litigation"},{"title":"2026 US trends: AI, securities and Delaware disputes - CDR News","url":"https://www.cdr-news.com/categories/litigation/2026-us-trends-ai-securities-and-delaware-disputes/"},{"title":"Inside the Courts – An Update From Skadden Securities Litigators | Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2025/02/inside-the-courts"},{"title":"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP - JDSupra","url":"https://www.jdsupra.com/legalnews/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-5893942/"},{"title":"M&A in the AI Era: What Buyers Can Do to Confirm and Protect Value | Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/sector-spotlights/ma-in-the-ai-era"},{"title":"Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom AI: Strategic Positioning in Legal AI - Klover.ai","url":"https://www.klover.ai/skadden-arps-slate-meagher-flom-ai-strategic-positioning-in-legal-ai/"},{"title":"Insights | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights?type=%7B0416A0AE-D175-4993-BBE0-6CF0CF7397DA%7D&capability=8551cacf-412c-4b5f-bfb4-000000037635&hassearched=true&panelid=tab-find-mode"},{"title":"Don’t Believe the Hype: Government Regulation of AI Continues to Advance | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/sector-spotlights/dont-believe-the-hype"}]},"I found Skadden's analysis of AI-related securities litigation trends for 2026. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overall Litigation Activity\n\nSecurities class action filings remained elevated in 2025, signaling that robust activity will likely persist into 2026.\n\n## AI and Emerging Trends\n\nCurrent securities litigation trends are likely to continue through 2026, with plaintiffs increasingly bringing suits over AI claims and private lending. Additionally, plaintiffs are also testing the limits of when expert opinions and short-seller reports can be credited at the motion-to-dismiss stage.\n\n## Private Credit Market\n\nPrivate credit lenders may become targets in securities class actions arising from capital raises involving retail investors. Plaintiffs have thus far treated private credit vehicles like traditional issuers under Rule 10b-5, focusing on alleged misstatements about portfolio performance and asset values.\n\n## Arbitration Clauses and Class Actions\n\nIf companies take advantage of the SEC's new openness to mandatory arbitration clauses, the securities litigation landscape could be altered, but the firm does not anticipate a flood of companies doing so at this stage. However, plaintiffs' attorneys have already indicated plans to challenge mandatory arbitration provisions if adopted.\n\nThe Skadden analysis emphasizes that the intersection of emerging technologies, regulatory shifts and evolving pleading strategies will present both challenges and opportunities for companies, investors and practitioners alike."],"durationSeconds":8.520569599999998}}
[2026-02-04T17:19:31.876Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUK9ksMxZNBhrsnEPusCLr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AI-washing securities class action lawsuits 2025 2026 false claims artificial intelligence\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI Washing: How Exaggerating Your (Artificial) Intelligence Can Get You and Your Business in Trouble\",\"url\":\"https://www.bfvlaw.com/ai-washing-how-exaggerating-your-artificial-intelligence-can-get-you-and-your-business-in-trouble/\"},{\"title\":\"Darrow · AI Washing Sparks Investor Suits and SEC Scrutiny\",\"url\":\"https://www.darrow.ai/resources/ai-washing\"},{\"title\":\"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch\"},{\"title\":\"AI-related securities class action filings are on the rise: Key observations | DLA Piper\",\"url\":\"https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/ai-related-securities-class-action-filings-are-on-the-rise-key-observations\"},{\"title\":\"Securities Suit Alleges AI-Washing Stock Price \\\"Pump\\\" | The D&O Diary\",\"url\":\"https://www.dandodiary.com/2026/02/articles/securities-litigation/securities-suit-alleges-ai-washing-stock-price-pump/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Infrastructure Company Hit with AI-Related Securities Suit | The D&O Diary\",\"url\":\"https://www.dandodiary.com/2026/01/articles/artificial-intelligence/ai-infrastructure-company-hit-with-ai-related-securities-suit/\"},{\"title\":\"More buzz than sting: The state of AI-related securities litigation\",\"url\":\"https://www.wtwco.com/en-us/insights/2025/11/more-buzz-than-sting-the-state-of-ai-related-securities-litigation\"},{\"title\":\"AI Washing Lawsuits and Investigations on the Rise\",\"url\":\"https://natlawreview.com/article/not-just-copyright-litigation-companies-increasingly-face-ai-washing-claims\"},{\"title\":\"Two Companies Hit with Separate AI-Washing Securities Lawsuits | The D&O Diary\",\"url\":\"https://www.dandodiary.com/2025/03/articles/securities-litigation/two-companies-hit-with-separate-ai-washing-securities-lawsuits/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding AI Washing and Securities Fraud Class Action Lawsuits\",\"url\":\"https://www.edelson-law.com/blog/2025/05/understanding-ai-washing-and-securites-fraud-class-action-lawsuits/\"}]\n\nBased on my search, here's a comprehensive overview of AI-washing securities class action lawsuits in 2025-2026:\n\n## Overview\n\nIn the last five years, more than 50 securities class action lawsuits have been filed alleging that defendants made false or misleading statements related to artificial intelligence (AI). The number of AI-related cases filed each year is trending upwards. While there were 7 securities class action cases related to AI disclosures filed in 2023, that number doubled to 14 in 2024, and 12 have been filed so far in 2025.\n\nSecurities class action filings remained elevated in 2025, signaling that robust activity will likely persist into 2026. AI-related class actions have outpaced other categories and are set to shape the litigation landscape in the coming year.\n\n## What is AI-Washing?\n\nA recurring theme in securities class action cases involving AI disclosures is that companies allegedly overstated the sophistication, effectiveness, or uniqueness of their AI, machine learning, or related technologies. In some cases, plaintiffs allege that companies concealed reliance on manual labor, third-party tools, or non-AI solutions while marketing offerings as AI-driven, a practice often dubbed \"AI washing.\"\n\n## Key Cases\n\n### Apple (June 2025)\nIn June 2025, shareholders filed a class action lawsuit (Tucker v. Apple Inc et al, U.S. District Court, Northern District of California, No. 25-05197) against the tech giant. According to the complaint, Apple's June 2024 Worldwide Developers Conference led the market to believe that AI would be a key driver of the upcoming iPhone 16. Yet Apple allegedly had no functional prototype of the advanced Siri features it was promoting. Apple's stock price plummeted, losing nearly one-quarter of its value (about $900 billion in market capitalization). The lawsuit alleges that Apple's AI claims amounted to securities fraud.\n\n### C3.ai (August 2025)\nC3.ai, Inc. faced a class action in August 2025 alleging it misled investors about the adoption and performance of its AI technology.\n\n### Innodata\nInnodata, Inc., a data engineering firm, is facing a federal securities class action brought on behalf of its shareholders. Wolfpack Research, a financial research firm, published a report unmasking \"smoke and mirrors\" AI and marketing claims.\n\n### Nate, Inc. (April 2025)\nIn April 2025, the SEC and DOJ jointly charged Albert Saniger, founder of Nate, Inc., after he raised more than $42 million by portraying his shopping app as AI-powered. In fact, transactions were being processed manually by overseas contractors, which has led to both civil and criminal proceedings.\n\n### CoreWeave (January 2026)\nEarlier in 2026, a plaintiff shareholder filed a securities class action lawsuit against AI infrastructure company CoreWeave. On January 12, 2026, a plaintiff shareholder filed a securities class action lawsuit in the District of New Jersey against CoreWeave and certain of its executives. The complaint purports to be filed on behalf of investors who purchased the company's securities between March 28, 2025, and December 15, 2025.\n\n### Richtech Robotics (February 2026)\nA new lawsuit alleges that Richtech Robotics used the announcement of a supposed AI-related \"collaboration\" with Microsoft allegedly to \"pump\" the company's share price just before disclosing an at-the-market private placement. This new lawsuit is just the latest in a recent series of securities class action lawsuits alleging share price pumping schemes.\n\n## Regulatory Enforcement\n\nThe SEC's Enforcement Division has named fraudulent AI claims an immediate priority, creating a dedicated Cybersecurity and Emerging Technologies Unit (CETU) in February 2025 to focus on AI-related misconduct. At a May 2025 enforcement forum, SEC officials stressed that staff are scrutinizing how companies describe their AI tech to investors.\n\nSince 2024, the U.S. Attorney's Office for the Southern District of New York has brought indictments for two executives for securities and wire fraud based on allegedly false and misleading statements about their companies' proprietary AI capabilities and revenues. The Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) and Federal Trade Commission (FTC) have also become more engaged in this space.\n\n## Settlement Data\n\nSeven of the AI-related lawsuits have been settled. But only one case filed after 2022 has been settled. The median settlement is $11.5 million. The average settlement is approximately $38.4 million; however, excluding the largest settlement ($189 million in a case involving issues relating to public safety), the average settlement drops to $13.3 million.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"a628cc6c-21c6-4acd-805b-31c67d09b7f8","tool_use_result":{"query":"AI-washing securities class action lawsuits 2025 2026 false claims artificial intelligence","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01W8r1cGXo2fk8qPFNTJ6sVv","content":[{"title":"AI Washing: How Exaggerating Your (Artificial) Intelligence Can Get You and Your Business in Trouble","url":"https://www.bfvlaw.com/ai-washing-how-exaggerating-your-artificial-intelligence-can-get-you-and-your-business-in-trouble/"},{"title":"Darrow · AI Washing Sparks Investor Suits and SEC Scrutiny","url":"https://www.darrow.ai/reso