[2026-02-04T17:24:20.504Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01Uk6N2G3VmLa1iseyR7n8sh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Research Complete\n\n**Verification Summary:** The original claim is **strongly verified**.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n1. **Litigation Surge Confirmed**: AI-washing securities class actions doubled from 7 (2023) to 14 (2024) to 12+ (2025), with 50+ total cases filed in five years. Median settlement: $11.5M.\n\n2. **Major Cases Filed 2024-2026**:\n   - **Apple** (June 2025): Alleged non-existent Siri AI capabilities at WWDC 2024\n   - **Nate Inc.** (April 2025): $42M raised claiming AI when automation was \"essentially zero\" - facing criminal charges\n   - **Richtech Robotics** (Feb 2026): Fabricated Microsoft \"collaboration\" to pump stock 44% before placement\n   - **CoreWeave** (Jan 2026): Concealed data center delays, $14B market cap loss\n   - **Innodata** (2024): Wolfpack Research exposed \"smoke and mirrors\" AI, 30% stock drop\n\n3. **Common AI-Washing Patterns**:\n   - Overstating AI sophistication/effectiveness\n   - Disguising manual labor as AI automation\n   - Misrepresenting legacy tech as AI-powered\n   - Fabricating partnerships with credible AI companies\n   - Timing claims around capital raises\n\n4. **Regulatory Response**: SEC established Cybersecurity and Emerging Technologies Unit (CETU) in February 2025, declaring AI-washing an \"immediate priority\"\n\n**Sources**: [Skadden](https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch), [SEC.gov](https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2024-36), [DLA Piper](https://www.dlapiper.com/en-us/insights/publications/2025/09/ai-related-securities-class-action-filings-are-on-the-rise-key-observations), [D&O Diary](https://www.dandodiary.com/2026/02/articles/securities-litigation/securities-suit-alleges-ai-washing-stock-price-pump/), [Harvard Law](https://corpgov.law.harvard.edu/2024/04/09/sec-fines-two-investment-advisers-for-ai-washing/)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12344,"cache_read_input_tokens":72187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12344},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"6a75840e-5eec-48c3-8759-efbc7841f9b4"}
